IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sgta-nouns`

-- INSTRUMENT: Telecommunications (Certificates of Competency for Ship Station Operators) Regulations (Cap. 323, Rg 1), 2002 Revised Edition,
-- made under section 74 of the Act (section 97 in the 2020 Revised Edition).  It governs the certificates that a radio operator on a ship
-- station must hold; the ship station licence is in Rg 5 (sgta-i-rg5-licences.l4).  It is not about receiving broadcasts.
-- Text: subjects/sg/telecommunications-ship-station-operators-regulations/registers/source-bundle/TA1999-RG1.txt.  IMDA's list has no
-- amending instrument for it; the Composition of Offences Regulations (sgta-i-comp.l4) name its offences as compoundable.
-- The First Schedule is the printed form of the certificate (no text in the PDF's text layer beyond its heading): not operative.

§ `Rg 1 regulation 2: definitions`

-- src:TA1999-RG1:38 | 2. In these Regulations, unless the context otherwise requires —
-- src:TA1999-RG1:39 | "certificate of competency" means a certificate of competency in radio-
-- src:TA1999-RG1:40 | communications issued under regulation 3;
-- src:TA1999-RG1:41 | "Constitution and Convention of the International Telecommunication Union"
-- src:TA1999-RG1:42 | means the Constitution and Convention of the International
-- src:TA1999-RG1:43 | Telecommunication Union signed at Geneva in 1992 and includes every
-- src:TA1999-RG1:44 | revision or modification thereof to which the Government is a party;
-- src:TA1999-RG1:45 | "International Convention for the Safety of Life at Sea" means the International
-- src:TA1999-RG1:46 | Convention signed at London on 1st November 1974 and the Regulations
-- src:TA1999-RG1:47 | annexed thereto, or a subsequent International Convention relating to the
-- src:TA1999-RG1:48 | safety of life at sea to which the Government is a party and every
-- src:TA1999-RG1:49 | regulation which may be annexed thereto;
-- src:TA1999-RG1:50 | "radio operator" means a person holding an appropriate certificate issued under
-- src:TA1999-RG1:51 | regulation 3 or an appropriate certificate recognised under regulation 12;
-- src:TA1999-RG1:52 | "Radio Regulations" means the Radio Regulations annexed to the Constitution
-- src:TA1999-RG1:53 | and Convention of the International Telecommunication Union and
-- src:TA1999-RG1:54 | includes every revision or modification thereof to which the Government
-- src:TA1999-RG1:55 | has ratified or accepted;
-- src:TA1999-RG1:56 | "ship" has the same meaning as in the Merchant Shipping Act (Cap. 179) and
-- src:TA1999-RG1:57 | includes an oil rig;
-- src:TA1999-RG1:58 | "ship station" means a station located on board a ship which is not permanently
-- src:TA1999-RG1:59 | moored;
-- src:TA1999-RG1:60 | "station" means a transmitter, receiver, a combination of transmitter and receiver
-- src:TA1999-RG1:61 | or any accessory thereto which is used or intended to be used for radio-
-- src:TA1999-RG1:62 | communication;
-- src:TA1999-RG1:63 | "STCW Code" means the Seafarer’s Training, Certification and Watchkeeping
-- src:TA1999-RG1:64 | Code adopted by the 1995 Conference of Practice to the International
-- src:TA1999-RG1:65 | Convention on Standards of Training, Certification and Watchkeeping for
-- src:TA1999-RG1:66 | Seafarers 1978, and any amendment thereto which has come into force
-- src:TA1999-RG1:67 | and has been accepted by the Government;
-- src:TA1999-RG1:68 | "STCW Convention" means the International Convention on Standards of
-- src:TA1999-RG1:69 | Training, Certification and Watchkeeping for Seafarers 1978, as amended
-- src:TA1999-RG1:70 | on 7th July 1995, and any amendment thereto which has come into force
-- src:TA1999-RG1:71 | and has been accepted by the Government.
@ref Rg 1 reg 2 (src:TA1999-RG1:38-71)
GIVEN `the person holds an appropriate certificate issued under regulation 3 or an appropriate certificate recognised under regulation 12` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 2: the person is a "radio operator"` MEANS
    `the person holds an appropriate certificate issued under regulation 3 or an appropriate certificate recognised under regulation 12`

GIVEN `it is a station located on board a ship which is not permanently moored` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 2: this is a "ship station"` MEANS
    `it is a station located on board a ship which is not permanently moored`

GIVEN `it is a ship within the meaning of the Merchant Shipping Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an oil rig` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 2: this is a "ship"` MEANS
    `it is a ship within the meaning of the Merchant Shipping Act` OR `it is an oil rig`

GIVEN `it is a certificate of competency in radio-communications issued under regulation 3` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 2: this is a "certificate of competency"` MEANS
    `it is a certificate of competency in radio-communications issued under regulation 3`

GIVEN `it is a transmitter, receiver, a combination of transmitter and receiver or any accessory used or intended to be used for radio-communication` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 2: this is a "station"` MEANS
    `it is a transmitter, receiver, a combination of transmitter and receiver or any accessory used or intended to be used for radio-communication`

GIVEN `it is the Constitution and Convention of the International Telecommunication Union signed at Geneva in 1992, or a revision or modification to which the Government is a party` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 2: this is the "Constitution and Convention of the International Telecommunication Union"` MEANS
    `it is the Constitution and Convention of the International Telecommunication Union signed at Geneva in 1992, or a revision or modification to which the Government is a party`

GIVEN `it is the International Convention signed at London on 1 November 1974, its annexed Regulations, or a later Convention on safety of life at sea to which the Government is a party` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 2: this is the "International Convention for the Safety of Life at Sea"` MEANS
    `it is the International Convention signed at London on 1 November 1974, its annexed Regulations, or a later Convention on safety of life at sea to which the Government is a party`

GIVEN `they are the Radio Regulations annexed to the Constitution and Convention of the International Telecommunication Union, or a revision or modification the Government has ratified or accepted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 2: these are the "Radio Regulations"` MEANS
    `they are the Radio Regulations annexed to the Constitution and Convention of the International Telecommunication Union, or a revision or modification the Government has ratified or accepted`

GIVEN `it is the Seafarer's Training, Certification and Watchkeeping Code adopted by the 1995 Conference of Parties, or an amendment in force and accepted by the Government` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 2: this is the "STCW Code"` MEANS
    `it is the Seafarer's Training, Certification and Watchkeeping Code adopted by the 1995 Conference of Parties, or an amendment in force and accepted by the Government`

GIVEN `it is the International Convention on Standards of Training, Certification and Watchkeeping for Seafarers 1978 as amended on 7 July 1995, or an amendment in force and accepted by the Government` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 2: this is the "STCW Convention"` MEANS
    `it is the International Convention on Standards of Training, Certification and Watchkeeping for Seafarers 1978 as amended on 7 July 1995, or an amendment in force and accepted by the Government`

§ `Rg 1 regulations 3 to 6: certificates, secrecy, examinations, fees`

-- src:TA1999-RG1:74 | 3. —(1) The Authority may issue a certificate of competency in radio-communications
-- src:TA1999-RG1:75 | to a person on being satisfied, after an examination referred to in regulation 5, that he is
-- src:TA1999-RG1:76 | qualified to hold the certificate of competency under these Regulations.
-- src:TA1999-RG1:77 | (2) The certificate of competency shall be in the form set out in the First Schedule and
-- src:TA1999-RG1:78 | graded as follows:
-- src:TA1999-RG1:79 | (a) General Operator’s Certificate of Competency; and
-- src:TA1999-RG1:80 | (b) Restricted Operator’s Certificate of Competency.
@ref Rg 1 reg 3 (src:TA1999-RG1:74-80)
GIVEN `the Authority is satisfied, after an examination under regulation 5, that the person is qualified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 3: the Authority may issue a certificate of competency in radio-communications to the person` MEANS
    `the Authority is satisfied, after an examination under regulation 5, that the person is qualified`

GIVEN grade IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 3(2): this is a grade of certificate of competency` MEANS
    elem grade (LIST "General Operator's Certificate of Competency", "Restricted Operator's Certificate of Competency")

-- src:TA1999-RG1:83 | 4. The holder of a certificate of competency shall make a declaration to the Authority, in
-- src:TA1999-RG1:84 | such form as the Authority may require, to preserve the secrecy of correspondence which
-- src:TA1999-RG1:85 | he may receive in the execution of his duties in such capacity.
@ref Rg 1 reg 4 (src:TA1999-RG1:83-85)
GIVEN `the holder made a declaration to the Authority, in the form it required, to preserve the secrecy of correspondence received in the execution of the holder's duties` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 4: the holder has made the declaration` MEANS
    `the holder made a declaration to the Authority, in the form it required, to preserve the secrecy of correspondence received in the execution of the holder's duties`

-- src:TA1999-RG1:87 | 5. —(1) The Authority may at any time, but not less than twice a year, hold such
-- src:TA1999-RG1:88 | examination for the grades of certificate of competency set out in regulation 3 (2) as the
-- src:TA1999-RG1:89 | Authority considers necessary.
-- src:TA1999-RG1:90 | (2) A candidate for an examination for a certificate of competency must —
-- src:TA1999-RG1:91 | (a) have attained the age of 18 years;
-- src:TA1999-RG1:92 | (b) furnish to the Authority 2 passport size photographs of himself and such
-- src:TA1999-RG1:93 | personal particulars as the Authority may require; and
-- src:TA1999-RG1:94 | (c) satisfy the Authority as to his medical fitness (including eyesight and hearing),
-- src:TA1999-RG1:95 | and hold a certificate issued by a medical practitioner registered under the
-- src:TA1999-RG1:96 | Medical Registration Act (Cap. 174) attesting to his medical fitness.
-- src:TA1999-RG1:97 | (3) The syllabus and other details of an examination for each grade of certificate of
-- src:TA1999-RG1:98 | competency may be obtained from the Authority on a written application made to the
-- src:TA1999-RG1:99 | Chief Executive.
@ref Rg 1 reg 5 (src:TA1999-RG1:87-99)
GIVEN `age in years` IS A NUMBER
      `the candidate furnished 2 passport size photographs and the personal particulars the Authority required` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the candidate satisfied the Authority as to medical fitness (eyesight and hearing) and holds a certificate of a registered medical practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 5(2): the candidate may sit the examination` MEANS
    (`age in years` AT LEAST 18) AND `the candidate furnished 2 passport size photographs and the personal particulars the Authority required` AND `the candidate satisfied the Authority as to medical fitness (eyesight and hearing) and holds a certificate of a registered medical practitioner`

GIVEN `times the Authority held the examination in the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 5(1): the Authority has held the examination as often as the regulation requires` MEANS
    `times the Authority held the examination in the year` AT LEAST 2

-- src:TA1999-RG1:102 | 6. The fees for —
-- src:TA1999-RG1:103 | (a) an examination for a certificate of competency;
-- src:TA1999-RG1:104 | (b) the issue of a certificate of competency; and
-- src:TA1999-RG1:105 | (c) the issue of a duplicate of a certificate of competency,
-- src:TA1999-RG1:106 | shall be as specified in the Second Schedule.
-- src:TA1999-RG1:291 | 1. For an examination for a General Operator’s Certificate of $100
-- src:TA1999-RG1:292 | Competency
-- src:TA1999-RG1:293 | 2. For an examination for a Restricted Operator’s Certificate of $ 70
-- src:TA1999-RG1:294 | Competency
-- src:TA1999-RG1:295 | 3. For the issue of a certificate of competency $ 10
-- src:TA1999-RG1:296 | 4. For the issue of a duplicate certificate of competency $5
-- src:TA1999-RG1:297 | 5. For the revalidation of a certificate of competency $ 10
-- src:TA1999-RG1:298 | 6. For the issue of a certificate of endorsement $ 18
-- src:TA1999-RG1:299 | 7. For the issue of a duplicate certificate of endorsement $ 18.
@ref Rg 1 reg 6 (src:TA1999-RG1:102-299)
GIVEN `item` IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Rg 1 reg 6 and Second Schedule: the fee in dollars` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `item` EQUALS "examination for a General Operator's Certificate of Competency" THEN JUST 100
           IF `item` EQUALS "examination for a Restricted Operator's Certificate of Competency" THEN JUST 70
           IF `item` EQUALS "issue of a certificate of competency" THEN JUST 10
           IF `item` EQUALS "issue of a duplicate certificate of competency" THEN JUST 5
           IF `item` EQUALS "revalidation of a certificate of competency" THEN JUST 10
           IF `item` EQUALS "issue of a certificate of endorsement" THEN JUST 18
           IF `item` EQUALS "issue of a duplicate certificate of endorsement" THEN JUST 18
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `Rg 1 regulations 7 to 11: the two grades and their authority, conventions and revalidation`

-- src:TA1999-RG1:109 | 7. In order to qualify for a General Operator’s Certificate of Competency, a candidate
-- src:TA1999-RG1:110 | shall give proof to the Authority by examination that he —
-- src:TA1999-RG1:111 | (a) has detailed practical knowledge of the operation of all the sub-systems and
-- src:TA1999-RG1:112 | equipment of the Global Maritime Distress and Safety System;
-- src:TA1999-RG1:113 | (b) has the ability to send and receive messages correctly by radio-telephone and
-- src:TA1999-RG1:114 | by direct-printing telegraphy;
-- src:TA1999-RG1:115 | (c) has detailed knowledge of the Radio Regulations relating to radio-
-- src:TA1999-RG1:116 | communications, and knowledge of the documents relating to charges for radio-
-- src:TA1999-RG1:117 | communications, and of the provisions of the International Convention for the
-- src:TA1999-RG1:118 | Safety of Life at Sea relating to radio-communications;
-- src:TA1999-RG1:119 | (d) has adequate knowledge of the English language as to be able to express
-- src:TA1999-RG1:120 | himself satisfactorily both orally and in writing; and
-- src:TA1999-RG1:121 | (e) satisfies the standard of competence specified in section A-IV/2 of the STCW
-- src:TA1999-RG1:122 | Code.
@ref Rg 1 reg 7 (src:TA1999-RG1:109-122)
GIVEN `the candidate showed by examination detailed practical knowledge of the operation of all the sub-systems and equipment of the Global Maritime Distress and Safety System` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the candidate showed the ability to send and receive messages correctly by radio-telephone and by direct-printing telegraphy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the candidate showed detailed knowledge of the Radio Regulations on radio-communications, the documents on charges and the Safety of Life at Sea provisions on radio-communications` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the candidate showed adequate knowledge of the English language to express himself satisfactorily orally and in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the candidate satisfied the standard of competence in section A-IV/2 of the STCW Code` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 7: the candidate qualifies for a General Operator's Certificate of Competency` MEANS
        `the candidate showed by examination detailed practical knowledge of the operation of all the sub-systems and equipment of the Global Maritime Distress and Safety System`
    AND `the candidate showed the ability to send and receive messages correctly by radio-telephone and by direct-printing telegraphy`
    AND `the candidate showed detailed knowledge of the Radio Regulations on radio-communications, the documents on charges and the Safety of Life at Sea provisions on radio-communications`
    AND `the candidate showed adequate knowledge of the English language to express himself satisfactorily orally and in writing`
    AND `the candidate satisfied the standard of competence in section A-IV/2 of the STCW Code`

-- src:TA1999-RG1:125 | 8. The holder of a General Operator’s Certificate of Competency is authorised to operate
-- src:TA1999-RG1:126 | the radio-communication services of a ship station which is —
-- src:TA1999-RG1:127 | (a) licensed under the Telecommunications (Radio-communication) Regulations
-- src:TA1999-RG1:128 | (Rg 5); and
-- src:TA1999-RG1:129 | (b) equipped with radio-communication apparatus in accordance with the
-- src:TA1999-RG1:130 | procedures laid down in the Radio Regulations for the Global Maritime Distress
-- src:TA1999-RG1:131 | and Safety System.
@ref Rg 1 reg 8 (src:TA1999-RG1:125-131)
GIVEN `the ship station is licensed under the Telecommunications (Radio-communication) Regulations (Rg 5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is equipped with radio-communication apparatus in accordance with the Radio Regulations procedures for the Global Maritime Distress and Safety System` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 8: the holder of a General Operator's Certificate of Competency is authorised to operate the radio-communication services of the ship station` MEANS
    `the ship station is licensed under the Telecommunications (Radio-communication) Regulations (Rg 5)` AND `it is equipped with radio-communication apparatus in accordance with the Radio Regulations procedures for the Global Maritime Distress and Safety System`

-- src:TA1999-RG1:134 | 9. In order to qualify for a Restricted Operator’s Certificate of Competency, a candidate
-- src:TA1999-RG1:135 | shall give proof to the Authority by examination that he —
-- src:TA1999-RG1:136 | (a) has practical knowledge of the operation of all the sub-systems and equipment
-- src:TA1999-RG1:137 | of the Global Maritime Distress and Safety System which is required while the
-- src:TA1999-RG1:138 | ship is sailing within the range of Very High Frequency coast stations;
-- src:TA1999-RG1:139 | (b) has the ability to send and receive messages correctly by radio-telephone;
-- src:TA1999-RG1:140 | (c) has knowledge of the Radio Regulations relating to radiotelephony
-- src:TA1999-RG1:141 | communications and specifically of the part of the Radio Regulations relating to
-- src:TA1999-RG1:142 | the safety of life;
-- src:TA1999-RG1:143 | (d) has elementary knowledge of the English language as to be able to express
-- src:TA1999-RG1:144 | himself satisfactorily both orally and in writing; and
-- src:TA1999-RG1:145 | (e) satisfies the standard of competence specified in section A-IV/2 of the STCW
-- src:TA1999-RG1:146 | Code.
@ref Rg 1 reg 9 (src:TA1999-RG1:134-146)
GIVEN `the candidate showed practical knowledge of the operation of the Global Maritime Distress and Safety System required while sailing within the range of Very High Frequency coast stations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the candidate showed the ability to send and receive messages correctly by radio-telephone` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the candidate showed knowledge of the Radio Regulations on radiotelephony communications and safety of life` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the candidate showed elementary knowledge of the English language to express himself satisfactorily orally and in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the candidate satisfied the standard of competence in section A-IV/2 of the STCW Code` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 9: the candidate qualifies for a Restricted Operator's Certificate of Competency` MEANS
        `the candidate showed practical knowledge of the operation of the Global Maritime Distress and Safety System required while sailing within the range of Very High Frequency coast stations`
    AND `the candidate showed the ability to send and receive messages correctly by radio-telephone`
    AND `the candidate showed knowledge of the Radio Regulations on radiotelephony communications and safety of life`
    AND `the candidate showed elementary knowledge of the English language to express himself satisfactorily orally and in writing`
    AND `the candidate satisfied the standard of competence in section A-IV/2 of the STCW Code`

-- src:TA1999-RG1:149 | 10. The holder of a Restricted Operator’s Certificate of Competency is authorised to
-- src:TA1999-RG1:150 | operate the radio-communication services of a ship station which is —
-- src:TA1999-RG1:151 | (a) licensed under the Telecommunications (Radio-communication) Regulations
-- src:TA1999-RG1:152 | (Rg 5); and
-- src:TA1999-RG1:153 | (b) equipped with radio-communication apparatus in accordance with the
-- src:TA1999-RG1:154 | procedures laid down in the Radio Regulations for the Global Maritime Distress
-- src:TA1999-RG1:155 | and Safety System.
@ref Rg 1 reg 10 (src:TA1999-RG1:149-155)
GIVEN `the ship station is licensed under the Telecommunications (Radio-communication) Regulations (Rg 5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is equipped with radio-communication apparatus in accordance with the Radio Regulations procedures for the Global Maritime Distress and Safety System` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 10: the holder of a Restricted Operator's Certificate of Competency is authorised to operate the radio-communication services of the ship station` MEANS
    `the ship station is licensed under the Telecommunications (Radio-communication) Regulations (Rg 5)` AND `it is equipped with radio-communication apparatus in accordance with the Radio Regulations procedures for the Global Maritime Distress and Safety System`

-- src:TA1999-RG1:158 | 11. —(1) All certificates of competency issued by the Authority shall be in accordance
-- src:TA1999-RG1:159 | with the Radio Regulations and the STCW Convention and shall be valid so long as the
-- src:TA1999-RG1:160 | Constitution and Convention of the International Telecommunication Union and the
-- src:TA1999-RG1:161 | STCW Convention remain in force.
-- src:TA1999-RG1:162 | (2) All certificates of competency shall be endorsed by the Authority in accordance with
-- src:TA1999-RG1:163 | Article VI of the STCW Convention and contain the information specified in paragraphs
-- src:TA1999-RG1:164 | 1 and 2 of section A-I/2 of the STCW Code.
-- src:TA1999-RG1:165 | (3) Notwithstanding anything in the Radio Regulations, the holder of a certificate of
-- src:TA1999-RG1:166 | competency who is serving at sea or intends to return to sea after a period ashore shall, in
-- src:TA1999-RG1:167 | order to continue to qualify for sea service as a radio operator, have his certificate of
-- src:TA1999-RG1:168 | competency revalidated by the Authority at intervals not exceeding 5 years from the date
-- src:TA1999-RG1:169 | of issue or revalidation, as the case may be.
-- src:TA1999-RG1:170 | (4) An application for revalidation under paragraph (3) shall be accompanied by the fee
-- src:TA1999-RG1:171 | specified in the Second Schedule.
-- src:TA1999-RG1:172 | (5) The Authority shall refuse to revalidate a certificate of competency under paragraph
-- src:TA1999-RG1:173 | (3) if the holder thereof does not show that he has satisfied the requirements of the STCW
-- src:TA1999-RG1:174 | Convention with regard to medical fitness and continued professional competence.
@ref Rg 1 reg 11 (src:TA1999-RG1:158-174)
GIVEN `years since the certificate was issued or last revalidated` IS A NUMBER
      `the holder is serving at sea or intends to return to sea after a period ashore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 11(3): the certificate must be revalidated to continue to qualify for sea service as a radio operator` MEANS
    `the holder is serving at sea or intends to return to sea after a period ashore` AND (`years since the certificate was issued or last revalidated` AT LEAST 5)

GIVEN `the holder shows satisfaction of the STCW Convention requirements on medical fitness and continued professional competence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 11(5): the Authority may revalidate the certificate of competency` MEANS
    `the holder shows satisfaction of the STCW Convention requirements on medical fitness and continued professional competence`

GIVEN `the certificate is in accordance with the Radio Regulations and the STCW Convention, endorsed under Article VI of the STCW Convention and contains the information section A-I/2 of the STCW Code specifies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 11(1) and (2): the certificate of competency is as the regulation requires` MEANS
    `the certificate is in accordance with the Radio Regulations and the STCW Convention, endorsed under Article VI of the STCW Convention and contains the information section A-I/2 of the STCW Code specifies`

§ `Rg 1 regulations 12 to 16: endorsement, disease, suspension, offences, savings`

-- src:TA1999-RG1:177 | 12. —(1) The Authority may, in its discretion and upon such conditions as it may
-- src:TA1999-RG1:178 | determine, recognise any valid certificate of competency issued by a foreign maritime
-- src:TA1999-RG1:179 | administration by issuing to the holder thereof a certificate of endorsement attesting the
-- src:TA1999-RG1:180 | recognition of the certificate in accordance with Regulation I/10 of the STCW
-- src:TA1999-RG1:181 | Convention.
-- src:TA1999-RG1:182 | (2) The certificate of endorsement referred to in paragraph (1) shall contain the
-- src:TA1999-RG1:183 | information specified in paragraph 3 of section A-I/2 of the STCW Code.
-- src:TA1999-RG1:184 | (3) The recognition of any certificate of competency issued by a foreign maritime
-- src:TA1999-RG1:185 | administration shall be subject to the following conditions:
-- src:TA1999-RG1:186 | (a) that the Authority is of the opinion that the certificate of competency is of a
-- src:TA1999-RG1:187 | grade appropriate to the capacity in which the holder thereof is to be employed on
-- src:TA1999-RG1:188 | a Singapore ship or is of a higher grade; and
-- src:TA1999-RG1:189 | (b) that the Authority is satisfied that the holder of the certificate of competency is
-- src:TA1999-RG1:190 | a fit and proper person to be employed on a Singapore ship.
-- src:TA1999-RG1:191 | (4) The fees for the issue of a certificate of endorsement and a duplicate thereof shall be
-- src:TA1999-RG1:192 | as specified in the Second Schedule.
-- src:TA1999-RG1:193 | (5) Where the Authority is of the opinion that the holder of a certificate of competency
-- src:TA1999-RG1:194 | recognised under this regulation is not a fit and proper person to be employed on a
-- src:TA1999-RG1:195 | Singapore ship or has breached any condition upon which his certificate is recognised,
-- src:TA1999-RG1:196 | the Authority may —
-- src:TA1999-RG1:197 | (a) issue a written notice to the holder informing him of its intention to cease
-- src:TA1999-RG1:198 | recognition of such certificate and give the reasons therefor; and
-- src:TA1999-RG1:199 | (b) require that person to show cause why his certificate should not cease to be
-- src:TA1999-RG1:200 | recognised.
-- src:TA1999-RG1:201 | (6) A holder of a certificate of competency who is required to show cause under
-- src:TA1999-RG1:202 | paragraph (5) may do so in writing addressed to the Authority or may, at the discretion of
-- src:TA1999-RG1:203 | the Authority, appear before an officer appointed by the Authority to investigate the
-- src:TA1999-RG1:204 | matter.
-- src:TA1999-RG1:205 | (7) Where no cause or insufficient cause is shown, the Authority may issue a written
-- src:TA1999-RG1:206 | notice to the holder of the certificate of competency informing him that the certificate of
-- src:TA1999-RG1:207 | competency shall cease to be recognised as from a specified date and giving the reasons
-- src:TA1999-RG1:208 | therefor and the holder shall, on being so required by the Authority, immediately deliver
-- src:TA1999-RG1:209 | his certificate of endorsement to the Authority for cancellation.
-- src:TA1999-RG1:210 | (8) Any person who fails to deliver his certificate of endorsement to the Authority when
-- src:TA1999-RG1:211 | required by the Authority to do so under paragraph (7) shall be guilty of an offence and
-- src:TA1999-RG1:212 | shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $2,000.
-- src:TA1999-RG1:213 | (9) Any person aggrieved by any decision of the Authority to cease recognition of his
-- src:TA1999-RG1:214 | certificate of competency may appeal to the Minister whose decision shall be final.
-- src:TA1999-RG1:215 | (10) No appeal lodged under paragraph (9) shall operate as a stay of the decision of the
-- src:TA1999-RG1:216 | Authority to cease recognition of the certificate of competency of the appellant except
-- src:TA1999-RG1:217 | with the written consent of the Authority.
@ref Rg 1 reg 12 (src:TA1999-RG1:177-217)
GIVEN `the certificate is of a grade appropriate to the capacity in which the holder is to be employed on a Singapore ship, or higher` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority is satisfied the holder is a fit and proper person to be employed on a Singapore ship` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 12(1) and (3): the Authority may recognise the foreign certificate of competency by a certificate of endorsement` MEANS
    `the certificate is of a grade appropriate to the capacity in which the holder is to be employed on a Singapore ship, or higher` AND `the Authority is satisfied the holder is a fit and proper person to be employed on a Singapore ship`

GIVEN `the Authority is of the opinion that the holder is not a fit and proper person, or has breached a condition of recognition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no cause or insufficient cause was shown after written notice to show cause` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 12(5) to (7): the Authority may give written notice that the certificate shall cease to be recognised from a specified date` MEANS
    `the Authority is of the opinion that the holder is not a fit and proper person, or has breached a condition of recognition` AND `no cause or insufficient cause was shown after written notice to show cause`

GIVEN `the holder failed to deliver the certificate of endorsement to the Authority when required` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Rg 1 reg 12(8): the most the fine may be on conviction, in dollars` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the holder failed to deliver the certificate of endorsement to the Authority when required` THEN JUST 2000 OTHERWISE NOTHING

GIVEN `the Authority gave written consent to a stay` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 12(9) and (10): the appeal to the Minister, whose decision is final, stays the Authority's decision` MEANS
    `the Authority gave written consent to a stay`

-- src:TA1999-RG1:220 | 13. —(1) The Authority may cancel or suspend any certificate of competency if the
-- src:TA1999-RG1:221 | holder thereof is suffering from a disease or disability which, in the opinion of the
-- src:TA1999-RG1:222 | Authority, makes him incapable of discharging his ordinary duties as a radio operator
-- src:TA1999-RG1:223 | adequately.
-- src:TA1999-RG1:224 | (2) The Authority shall not cancel or suspend any certificate of competency until the
-- src:TA1999-RG1:225 | radio operator concerned has been notified in writing to appear before the Authority to
-- src:TA1999-RG1:226 | show cause why his certificate should not be cancelled or suspended.
-- src:TA1999-RG1:227 | (3) The certificate of competency of a radio operator who appears to show cause is to be
-- src:TA1999-RG1:228 | suspended until the decision of the Authority has been made known.
-- src:TA1999-RG1:229 | (4) Where the radio operator fails to appear before the Authority, the Authority shall
-- src:TA1999-RG1:230 | immediately cancel his certificate of competency.
@ref Rg 1 reg 13 (src:TA1999-RG1:220-230)
GIVEN `the holder is suffering from a disease or disability that in the Authority's opinion makes him incapable of discharging his ordinary duties as a radio operator adequately` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the holder was notified in writing to appear before the Authority to show cause` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the holder failed to appear` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 13: the Authority may cancel or suspend the certificate of competency` MEANS
    `the holder failed to appear`
    OR (`the holder is suffering from a disease or disability that in the Authority's opinion makes him incapable of discharging his ordinary duties as a radio operator adequately` AND `the holder was notified in writing to appear before the Authority to show cause`)

-- src:TA1999-RG1:233 | 14. —(1) Notwithstanding regulation 13, a certificate of competency may be suspended
-- src:TA1999-RG1:234 | at any time on any ground which the Authority considers sufficient.
-- src:TA1999-RG1:235 | (2) The holder of a certificate of competency shall return the certificate to the Authority
-- src:TA1999-RG1:236 | upon receiving notice in writing from the Authority of its suspension.
@ref Rg 1 reg 14 (src:TA1999-RG1:233-236)
GIVEN `the Authority considers the ground sufficient` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 14: the certificate of competency may be suspended at any time` MEANS
    `the Authority considers the ground sufficient`

-- src:TA1999-RG1:239 | 15. —(1) Any person who forges or fraudulently alters, or knowingly assists in forging
-- src:TA1999-RG1:240 | or fraudulently altering, or knowingly causes or permits to be forged or fraudulently
-- src:TA1999-RG1:241 | altered, any of the following shall be guilty of an offence:
-- src:TA1999-RG1:242 | (a) any declaration made under regulation 4;
-- src:TA1999-RG1:243 | (b) any certificate or other document issued under these Regulations, or any entry
-- src:TA1999-RG1:244 | or endorsement prescribed by these Regulations to be made in or on such
-- src:TA1999-RG1:245 | certificate or other document; or
-- src:TA1999-RG1:246 | (c) any document which the person produces to the Authority or its agent for the
-- src:TA1999-RG1:247 | purposes of obtaining for himself or any other person any certificate or other
-- src:TA1999-RG1:248 | document under these Regulations or any entry or endorsement in or on such
-- src:TA1999-RG1:249 | certificate or other document.
-- src:TA1999-RG1:250 | (2) Any person who fraudulently or dishonestly uses, or knowingly permits or causes
-- src:TA1999-RG1:251 | any other person to fraudulently or dishonestly use —
-- src:TA1999-RG1:252 | (a) any declaration, certificate or other document referred to in paragraph (1) (a),
-- src:TA1999-RG1:253 | (b) or (c) which has been forged or fraudulently altered, or which is otherwise
-- src:TA1999-RG1:254 | false or misleading in any material particular; or
-- src:TA1999-RG1:255 | (b) any certificate or other document referred to in paragraph (1) (b) which has
-- src:TA1999-RG1:256 | expired, or has been cancelled or suspended, or has become invalid for any other
-- src:TA1999-RG1:257 | reason,
-- src:TA1999-RG1:258 | shall be guilty of an offence.
-- src:TA1999-RG1:259 | (3) Any person who, knowingly or recklessly for any purpose under these Regulations
-- src:TA1999-RG1:261 | (a) makes any statement or representation; or
-- src:TA1999-RG1:262 | (b) provides any information,
-- src:TA1999-RG1:263 | to the Authority or its agent which is false or misleading in any material particular shall
-- src:TA1999-RG1:264 | be guilty of an offence.
@ref Rg 1 reg 15 (src:TA1999-RG1:239-264)
GIVEN `the person forges or fraudulently alters, or knowingly assists, causes or permits the forging or fraudulent alteration of, a declaration, certificate or document issued or produced under the Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person fraudulently or dishonestly uses, or knowingly permits or causes another to use, a forged, altered, false, expired, cancelled or suspended document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knowingly or recklessly makes a statement or provides information to the Authority that is false or misleading in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 15: the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    `the person forges or fraudulently alters, or knowingly assists, causes or permits the forging or fraudulent alteration of, a declaration, certificate or document issued or produced under the Regulations`
    OR `the person fraudulently or dishonestly uses, or knowingly permits or causes another to use, a forged, altered, false, expired, cancelled or suspended document`
    OR `the person knowingly or recklessly makes a statement or provides information to the Authority that is false or misleading in a material particular`

-- src:TA1999-RG1:267 | 16. —(1) A certificate of competency in radio-communications issued under the
-- src:TA1999-RG1:268 | revoked Radio-communication (Certificates of Competency for Ship Station Operators)
-- src:TA1999-RG1:269 | Regulations (Rg 2, 1999 Ed.) shall be deemed to be a certificate of competency issued
-- src:TA1999-RG1:270 | under these Regulations.
-- src:TA1999-RG1:271 | (2) Notwithstanding regulation 16 and subject to paragraphs (3) and (4), a Certificate of
-- src:TA1999-RG1:272 | Competency in radio-communications, radiography or radiotelephony issued under the
-- src:TA1999-RG1:273 | revoked Radio-communication (Certificates of Competency for Ship Station Operators)
-- src:TA1999-RG1:274 | Regulations (Rg 2, 1996 Ed.) shall entitle the holder thereof to perform all the acts for
-- src:TA1999-RG1:275 | which he was authorised under the Certificate to perform as if these Regulations had not
-- src:TA1999-RG1:276 | been enacted.
-- src:TA1999-RG1:277 | (3) The Authority may, by notice in writing to the holder of any certificate referred to in
-- src:TA1999-RG1:278 | paragraph (2), cancel or revoke the certificate.
-- src:TA1999-RG1:279 | (4) Any certificates referred to in paragraph (2) shall not be valid after 1st February
-- src:TA1999-RG1:280 | 2002.
@ref Rg 1 reg 16 (src:TA1999-RG1:267-280)
GIVEN `the certificate was issued under the revoked Radio-communication (Certificates of Competency for Ship Station Operators) Regulations (Rg 2, 1999 Ed.)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 16(1): the certificate is deemed to be issued under these Regulations` MEANS
    `the certificate was issued under the revoked Radio-communication (Certificates of Competency for Ship Station Operators) Regulations (Rg 2, 1999 Ed.)`

GIVEN `the certificate was issued under the revoked Regulations (Rg 2, 1996 Ed.)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority has cancelled or revoked it by written notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date is after 1 February 2002` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 16(2) to (4): the certificate still entitles the holder to perform all the acts for which it authorised` MEANS
    `the certificate was issued under the revoked Regulations (Rg 2, 1996 Ed.)` AND (NOT `the Authority has cancelled or revoked it by written notice`) AND (NOT `the date is after 1 February 2002`)
